From: behery <behery@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 10:07:55 -0700
Subject: [MediaCapture] Deactivate SCContentSharingPicker after screenshot
 capture and clean up callbacks

When taking a screenshot on macOS via NativeScreenCapturePickerMac
(SCContentSharingPicker), such as when taking an entire-screen or window
screenshot in OmniboxEverywhere, the picker was set to active in Open(),
but never deactivated after the one-shot frame capture completed because
Close() is only called for long-running video streams. This left the
green/purple screen recording menu bar indicators active in macOS.

Clicking this lingering indicator re-invoked the system picker UI on
nothing. If the user then clicked "Cancel", Chrome crashed because stale
cancel callbacks were not cleared upon the original successful selection, causing a duplicate invocation of the one-shot Mojo response
callback.

This CL:
1. Adds MaybeDeactivatePicker helper to deactivate
   SCContentSharingPicker when no active streams exist, invoked on
   screenshot completion, cancellation, error, and stream close.
2. Cleans up the session content filter upon screenshot completion.
3. Resets remaining mutual-exclusion callbacks in
   OnPickerObserverUpdated, OnPickerObserverCancelled, and
   OnPickerObserverEncounteredError.
4. Updates unit tests to verify picker deactivation on screenshot
   capture and cancellation.

Bug: 555215271
Change-Id: I566c4bafe39a46a7ee17bb37819a219b5604b542
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8324087
Reviewed-by: Tove Petersson <tovep@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Hamzah Behery <behery@chromium.org>
